{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Or if he is informed.</b> The verse says ״or״ — because it first said ״ואשם״ (and he becomes guilty), and they of blessed memory (Torat Kohanim 4:23) taught that this indicates he brings an אשם תלוי (suspensive guilt-offering) if he is in doubt. Therefore it says ״or if he is informed״ — meaning, if it was certainly made known to him."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:53:06.984032864Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}